@startuml
!theme plain
title P1 Generic Media Ingest and Storage - Ingest Sequence

actor "Pulsar App" as App
participant "Upload Session API" as API
participant "Quota + Idempotency Gate" as Gate
participant "SubmitMedia" as Submit
database "SQLite" as DB
collections "Temp Storage" as Temp
participant "ffprobe + Signature Probe" as Probe
participant "ffmpeg" as FFmpeg
collections "Canonical WAV Storage" as Canon
participant "Legacy Voice Mapper" as Legacy
actor "Telegram Bot" as Tg

== App path ==
App -> API : POST /v1/media/uploads\ncontrol token + idempotency key
API -> Gate : check rate/concurrency/daily bytes
Gate -> DB : create upload session + processing media row
API --> App : upload id + scoped upload token

App -> API : PUT /v1/media/uploads/{id}\nresume/retry bytes
API -> Temp : append verified chunk(s)
API -> Submit : finalize when upload complete
Submit -> Probe : magic bytes + ffprobe(timeout)

alt valid phase-1 clip
  Submit -> FFmpeg : normalize to PCM s16le 44.1 kHz stereo WAV
  FFmpeg -> Canon : write canonical WAV
  Submit -> DB : mark ready\nhash/duration/loudness/size
  Submit -> Temp : delete upload bytes
  Submit -> Legacy : optional WAV compatibility mapping
else corrupt / unsupported / oversized / timed out
  Submit -> DB : mark failed\nnever expose ready media
end

alt repeated idempotency key
  App -> API : retry same create/finalize request
  API -> DB : lookup prior result
  API --> App : return original upload/media outcome
end

== Telegram path ==
Tg -> Submit : source=telegram raw file
Submit -> Temp : store downloaded raw bytes
Submit -> Probe : same validation path
Submit -> FFmpeg : same canonicalization path
Submit -> Legacy : preserve legacy queue/WAV behavior

note over Submit,Legacy
  App and Telegram must converge on the same validation,
  quota, retention, and status model. Telegram keeps its
  current acceptance ordering through the compatibility mapper.
end note

@enduml
